# Platform Channels Rule

Use when adding native iOS/Android functionality via Flutter platform channels (no third-party Dart packages).

## Architecture

- **Dart**: `MethodChannel` invokes native methods
- **iOS**: `ios/Classes/MasterfabricCorePlugin.swift` - FlutterMethodChannel
- **Android**: `android/.../MasterfabricCorePlugin.kt` - MethodChannel

## Existing Channels

| Channel Name | Purpose |
|--------------|---------|
| `com.masterfabric.app_tracking_transparency` | iOS ATT dialog, tracking status |
| `com.masterfabric.permission_helper` | Runtime permissions (camera, location, etc.) |

## Dart Side

```dart
import 'package:flutter/services.dart';

class MyNativeHelper {
  static const _channel = MethodChannel('com.masterfabric.my_feature');

  Future<bool> callNative() async {
    try {
      final result = await _channel.invokeMethod<bool>('methodName', args);
      return result ?? false;
    } on PlatformException catch (e) {
      debugPrint('❌ Platform error: ${e.code} - ${e.message}');
      return false;
    }
  }
}
```

## iOS (Swift)

```swift
// In MasterfabricCorePlugin.swift - register channel
let myChannel = FlutterMethodChannel(
  name: "com.masterfabric.my_feature",
  binaryMessenger: registrar.messenger()
)
registrar.addMethodCallDelegate(instance, channel: myChannel)

// Handle method
case "methodName":
  myMethod(result: result)
```

## Android (Kotlin)

```kotlin
// In MasterfabricCorePlugin.kt
channel = MethodChannel(binding.binaryMessenger, "com.masterfabric.my_feature")
channel.setMethodCallHandler(this)

override fun onMethodCall(call: MethodCall, result: Result) {
  when (call.method) {
    "methodName" -> myMethod(result)
    else -> result.notImplemented()
  }
}
```

## Platform Checks in Dart

Always guard channel calls:

```dart
if (kIsWeb) return null;  // Channels not available on web
try {
  return await _channel.invokeMethod('method', args);
} on PlatformException catch (e) {
  debugPrint('❌ ${e.code}: ${e.message}');
  return null;
}
```

## Plugin Registration

- iOS: Plugin registered in `GeneratedPluginRegistrant` via pubspec
- Android: Plugin in `MainActivity` / `FlutterEngine`
- Both channels can be registered in same plugin class

## Checklist

- [ ] Channel name: `com.masterfabric.[feature]` (reverse domain)
- [ ] Handle PlatformException in Dart
- [ ] Platform check (kIsWeb) before channel call
- [ ] iOS: Add usage descriptions to Info.plist (permissions)
- [ ] Android: Add uses-permission to AndroidManifest.xml
- [ ] Return safe defaults on error
